{
 "units": [
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-4a9062e93f2546589ba9b0cb9029e5d9",
   "title": "Initial Brief",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Debugging issues in the old pipeline took half a day each time.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t000",
       "char_start": 159,
       "char_end": 166
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The pipeline must stay compatible with Python 3.10, without using syntax introduced in 3.11+.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t000",
       "char_start": 227,
       "char_end": 261
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The assistant plans to first inspect the directory structure, main flow code, and target table schema.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t001",
       "char_start": 166,
       "char_end": 200
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t000",
    "synth-c3-t001"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-78cb3974009b4a88822808fd38e8673c",
   "title": "Code Survey",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The cron job triggers the import via etl.importer daily at 01:30.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t002",
       "char_start": 375,
       "char_end": 415
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The target database table is supplier_orders as defined in config.ini.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t002",
       "char_start": 601,
       "char_end": 616
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The main logic resides in etl/importer.py which is 842 lines long.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t003",
       "char_start": 12,
       "char_end": 37
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t002",
    "synth-c3-t003"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-0b8ab9bb9eb3401cb0af8c2b1783f6bf",
   "title": "Code Problems",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The legacy directory must not be modified in any way, not even formatting.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t004",
       "char_start": 42,
       "char_end": 63
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The assistant confirms that legacy files will be left untouched.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t005",
       "char_start": 3,
       "char_end": 23
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The insert_rows function builds SQL via string formatting, making it vulnerable to injection.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t006",
       "char_start": 1194,
       "char_end": 1262
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The clean_row uses a bare except that swallows all errors and only increments a global BAD_ROWS counter.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t007",
       "char_start": 63,
       "char_end": 108
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t004",
    "synth-c3-t005",
    "synth-c3-t006",
    "synth-c3-t007"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-a09f473628e34d5fa7cfdd55421bb72b",
   "title": "Schema Rules",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The existing supplier_orders columns must keep their names and types to avoid breaking a downstream financial report script.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t008",
       "char_start": 37,
       "char_end": 70
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t008"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-2b2d7f043ea146e6a9d2d2c094e5fc48",
   "title": "Refactor Plan",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The assistant proposes splitting the pipeline into reader, cleaner, writer modules and adding a supplier_orders_rejects table for bad rows.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t009",
       "char_start": 61,
       "char_end": 150
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t009"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-9ccec984e334417292a598335cff5013",
   "title": "Param & Deps",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "All SQL must use parameterized queries, including read statements, due to a security audit requirement.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t010",
       "char_start": 28,
       "char_end": 66
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The assistant confirms that psycopg2's parameter binding will be used everywhere, with no SQL string concatenation.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t011",
       "char_start": 52,
       "char_end": 112
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "No new third-party dependencies are allowed; only stdlib and the existing psycopg2 can be used.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t012",
       "char_start": 45,
       "char_end": 88
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The cleaning layer will use pure stdlib with decimal.Decimal for amounts and generator batches of 5000 rows.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t013",
       "char_start": 41,
       "char_end": 114
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t010",
    "synth-c3-t011",
    "synth-c3-t012",
    "synth-c3-t013"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-61a3d0bfdc5244b68d448b06cb908e18",
   "title": "Migration & Con",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The current schema is v2, and all migrations must be run with --lock to avoid breaking the pg_partman maintenance state.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t014",
       "char_start": 175,
       "char_end": 256
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The assistant plans to create a supplier_orders_rejects table without foreign keys, using a formal dbtool migrate --lock.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t015",
       "char_start": 83,
       "char_end": 159
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Only 5 database connections are allowed; exceeding them causes a silent firewall drop.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t016",
       "char_start": 22,
       "char_end": 60
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t014",
    "synth-c3-t015",
    "synth-c3-t016"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-6901e56f63f14da1b4cf4ba34bf49c9e",
   "title": "Implementation",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The pipeline will reuse a single connection, peaking at 1 out of the 5 limit.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t017",
       "char_start": 14,
       "char_end": 65
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The migration file and writer.py are written, using parameterized INSERT and execute_values.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t018",
       "char_start": 527,
       "char_end": 575
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t017",
    "synth-c3-t018"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-52dde244645b499bb3e24c5205bc6e8d",
   "title": "Encoding Issue",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The assistant initially suggests simplifying encoding to UTF‑8 with replace, but the user forbids it because vendor files are still in GBK.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t020",
       "char_start": 29,
       "char_end": 82
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The original sniff_encoding logic is preserved unchanged in etl/reader.py.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t021",
       "char_start": 53,
       "char_end": 108
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t019",
    "synth-c3-t020",
    "synth-c3-t021"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-31a1e90603e740cb82885b0c6e7c9c85",
   "title": "Maint & Privacy",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The staging run fails because the cluster requires maintenance mode before bulk copy.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t022",
       "char_start": 614,
       "char_end": 733
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The pipeline now enables maintenance mode before writing and disables it afterwards, aborting if enabling fails.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t023",
       "char_start": 59,
       "char_end": 170
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Phone numbers must never appear in logs; they can only be stored in the access‑controlled rejects table.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t024",
       "char_start": 35,
       "char_end": 63
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The cleaner only logs field names and failure types, and DEBUG‑level sampling masks phone columns with 138****.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t025",
       "char_start": 153,
       "char_end": 202
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t022",
    "synth-c3-t023",
    "synth-c3-t024",
    "synth-c3-t025"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-d3d57af105fd4853999e0bccfe5a1421",
   "title": "Cron Schedule",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "A full staging run succeeded: 4982 rows loaded, 18 rejects stored, peak DB connection of 1.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t026",
       "char_start": 1039,
       "char_end": 1076
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The assistant proposes moving the cron time to 02:30, but the user explains that 02:00‑04:00 is a backup window and suggests after 04:30.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t028",
       "char_start": 21,
       "char_end": 54
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c3-t026",
    "synth-c3-t027",
    "synth-c3-t028"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c3-t035"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-4cb6609847134b33b50d40e04d682d16",
   "title": "Testing & Recap",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Initial tests had two failures; one due to an incorrect test sample and one due to an expected outcome that wrongly treated negative amounts as invalid.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t030",
       "char_start": 220,
       "char_end": 256
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "After fixing the tests, all 25 test cases passed and a compileall check confirmed Python 3.10 compatibility.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t032",
       "char_start": 101,
       "char_end": 168
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Final verification showed no SQL concatenation, only one third‑party import (psycopg2), and no changes to the legacy directory.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t033",
       "char_start": 437,
       "char_end": 475
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The assistant provides a final checklist confirming all constraints are met and the cron time is set to 04:45.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c3-t035",
       "char_start": 311,
       "char_end": 343
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
